    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d493">

                <pb facs="0661" n="569" xml:id="pg569"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 800.24/57</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-13T23:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 13, 1918, 11 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 14, 3 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3875. For Crosby from Cravath:</p>
                <p>No. 230. Both French and British Governments are very anxious that proposed
                    Inter-Allied Munitions Council should be organized as promptly as possible in
                    order to insure early settlement of important questions, including more adequate
                    provision for munition needs of Italy. Loucheur has
                    received no answer to his cable on the subject communicated to our Government
                    through French Ambassador about April 15.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d493-f1"/>
                    Meantime, French, British and Italian Governments have made their designations
                    who are: Churchill, Minister of
                    Munitions, Sir Charles Ellis,
                        Layton [of Ministry of Munitions], and also a
                    representative of the War Office. French and Italians have designated
                    representatives of substantially corresponding rank; it is hoped that
                    corresponding designation will be made by our Government if principle of
                    organization approved at Washington. It is especially desired that our
                    delegation shall include one representative permanently resident in Paris.</p>
                <p>If principle of our representation approved, suggest advisability of early
                    organization with temporary attendance on behalf of our Government by General Pershing representatives, and by
                    representatives of our Council<anchor n="2" xml:id="d493-f2"/> and Maritime
                    Council.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sharp</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d493-f1" n="1" xml:id="d493-f1-content">
                <p>The French Ambassador’s note, actually dated Apr. 27, is printed, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg565">p. 565</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d493-f2" n="2" xml:id="d493-f2-content">
                <p>Inter-Allied Council on War Purchases and Finance.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
